[TEXT] I have all the evidence needed. The picture is crystal clear:

- **router0.eth0.10** (gateway 172.16.10.1) is UP and correctly addressed — the gateway itself is healthy.
- **mswitch1.eth4.10** (toward router0) is UP — the mswitch1→router0 VLAN 10 segment is fine.
- **mswitch1.eth0.10** (toward switch1, the access side) is **administratively DOWN** — flags `<BROADCAST,MULTICAST>`, no `UP`, state `DOWN`.
- **mswitch1.eth0.20** is UP — explaining why laptop0 on VLAN 20 is completely unaffected.

The trunk sub-interface for VLAN 10 on the switch1-facing port of mswitch1 has been shut down, severing VLAN 10 at exactly that hop.

